    <profile name="Repressor" typeId="2fae-b053-3f78-e7b2" typeName="Vehicle" hidden="false" id="349f-715e-9e89-5528">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="e555-4aed-dfcc-c0b4">Vehicle (Transport)</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Move" typeId="3614-4a2d-bffb-90e4">14</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="51fb-b7d9-aa59-863d">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Front" typeId="0ef8-a648-01d0-08ee">13</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Side" typeId="f150-c0dc-c192-9cb3">13</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Rear" typeId="8d4e-2aea-fffc-d556">10</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="HP" typeId="a76c-83b1-602f-9e62">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Transport Capacity" typeId="0c90-79e2-f768-e547">12</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Access Points" typeId="e217-1b1e-9494-3e3e">A Sororitas Repressor has one Access Point on each side of the hull and one at the rear.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Armoured Container" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="cbcf-b59d-1b11-1b5f">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with this upgrade reduces its Transport Capacity to 12 and gain the Infantry Transport special rule, but increases its Side Armour and Rear Armour by +1, up to a maximum of 12. Additionally, a model with this upgrade may take up to two additional Pintle Mounted heavy stubbers at a cost of +5 points each</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Armorium Cherub" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="8d3b-d6bc-a1d4-778b">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">If a unit is upgraded with an Armorium Cherub, place an Armorium Cherub token next to it representing the cherub; the token is only used for the purpose of this special rules and is ignored for all other game rules.
Once per battle, when the unit with the Armorium Cherub makes a Shooting Attack in the controlling player’s Shooting phase, the controlling player can remove an Armorium Cherub token from the unit if it has any. If they do, all To Hit rolls of 1 for that shooting attack are re-rolled</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Laud Hailer" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="ddfa-2517-6340-0007">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model equipped with a Laud Hailer has the Fear (1) special rule. In addition, friendly units with the Adeptus Ministorum faction that are within 12” of a model with a Laud Hailer are immune to the effects of Fear. A Laud Hailer is not considered a weapon and cannot be targeted by the Weapon Destroyed result on the Vehicle Damage Table.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Incensor Cherub" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="50ba-8efc-448e-e908" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="93">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">If a unit is upgraded with an Incensor Cherub, place an Incensor Cherub token next to it representing the cherub; the token is only used for the purpose of this special rules and is ignored for all other game rules.
Once per battle, when the unit with the Incensor Cherub fails an Act of Faith test, the controlling player can remove the token. If they do, the test can be re-rolled.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Simulacrum Imperialis" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="f409-24c3-6290-b5d9" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="94">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A unit that includes at least one model with a Simulacrum Imperialis adds +1 to the Wounds score used to decide if they win a Combat in the Assault phase. Additionally, a unit that includes at least one model with a Simulacrum Imperialis counts its Leadership characteristic as being 1 higher than it is, to a maximum of 10, when attempting Acts of Faith.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Makeshift Walker" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="3f5f-79b1-286c-2f78" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="93">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with a Makeshift Walker that chooses to Run gains the Shrouded (5+) special rule until the start of the controlling player’s next turn.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Nuncio-Vox" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="71ba-1459-a959-3e81" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="93">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">While at least one model with a nuncio-vox is present on the battlefield and not Embarked in a Vehicle or Building, the controlling player may re-roll any Scatter rolls made (whether as part of a weapon attack or the deployment of a model or unit), as long as the model with the nuncio-vox has line of sight to the unit targeted by the attack or the point chosen as the target of the deployment. In addition, a unit that includes at least one model with a nuncio-vox ignores the -1 penalty to Leadership imposed by the Night Fighting rules.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Ministorum Vexilla" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="fb1a-42d0-d792-f634" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="93">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A unit that includes at least one model with an Ministorum Vexilla adds +1 to the Wounds score used to decide if they win a Combat in the Assault phase.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Paragon Warsuit" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="6488-6b53-04e0-45c8" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="93">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with a Paragon Warsuit has a 2+ armour save.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Penitent Engine" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="94fb-ab58-952a-84b3" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="93">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with a Penitent Engine has a 4+ armour save. If a unit that includes only models with Penitent Engines fails a Morale check it does not Fall Back as per the standard rules, but instead suffers D3 automatic Wounds with no Saves or damage mitigation rolls of any kind allowed.
A unit that includes any model with Penitent Engines may not be joined by any models, or have any models assigned to it, unless that model is also equipped with a Penitent Engine.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Seraph Jump Pack" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="f4c9-126e-8107-5fbe" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="93">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">At the start of the controlling player’s Movement phase, a model with a Seraph jump pack may set its Move Characteristic to a value of 14 for the duration of the controlling player’s turn (sometimes referred to as ‘activating’ the jump pack). This allows a model with a Seraph jump pack to move up to 14”, regardless of the Movement Characteristic shown on its profile and gain any other benefits of a Movement Characteristic 
of 14 (including the bonus to Charge distance). In addition, all models with a Seraph jump pack that have been activated ignore terrain while Moving and Charging, but must take Dangerous Terrain tests as normal when beginning or ending their Movement in Dangerous Terrain. A model with an activated Seraph jump pack treats all Difficult Terrain as Dangerous Terrain and may move over both friendly and enemy models or units without penalty – but must end its 
Movement at least 1” away from any model from another unit.
A model with a Seraph jump pack may still Run if it would normally be able to Run. When making a Run move for a model with a Seraph jump pack, add the Initiative Characteristic of that model to 14 to determine how far it may move – the model ignores terrain and models from other units while making a Run move with a Seraph jump pack as previously noted, but may not make Shooting Attacks or declare a Charge in the same turn in which it has Run as per 
the normal rules for Running.
Any model with a Seraph jump pack also gains the Bulky (2) and Deep Strike special rules. In addition, a model with a Seraph Jump Pack and the Shield of Faith (X) special rule changes the value X of its Shield of Faith (X) to 5+, unless it would normally be better.
During a Reaction made in any Phase, a player may not choose to activate a model’s Seraph Jump Pack to gain any bonus to its Movement Characteristic</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Vehicle Fire Point (Arc, X)" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="86fd-c791-3674-0dba" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="94">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A Vehicle Fire Point is a mount that does not include any weapons, instead it allows models Embarked upon the Transport to fire the weapons they are equipped with from the Vehicle. A Vehicle Fire Point will note in brackets both the arc into which it can fire as well as the number of embarked models that can fire from it. Each embarked model firing from a Fire Point measures its range and line of sight from the opening on the model that denote the Fire Point and may fire one Ranged weapon it is equipped with as per the normal rules for Shooting. All weapons used by Embarked models are counted as being Defensive Weapons, regardless of their Strength.
Embarked models count as having moved for the purpose of shooting from Vehicle Fire Points if their Transport moved at Combat Speed during the previous Movement phase, and may only fire Snap Shots if their Transport moved at Cruising Speed.
Note that a Vehicle Fire Point is not itself a weapon and may not be targeted by the Weapon Destroyed result on the Vehicle Damage Chart.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Immolator" typeId="2fae-b053-3f78-e7b2" typeName="Vehicle" hidden="false" id="c915-48a5-c857-d94e">
