    <profile name="Hallowed Storm Shield" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="715e-85cf-0ee8-916d" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="92">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A Hallowed Storm Shield confers a 4+ Invulnerable Save. Invulnerable Saves granted by a Hallowed Storm Shield do not stack with other Invulnerable Saves. If a model equipped with a Hallowed Storm Shield also has the Shield of Faith (X) special rule, the Hallowed Storm Shield instead changes the value in brackets of that special rule to 4+.
A model with a Hallowed Storm Shield may not claim an additional attack for a second weapon in close combat or make attacks with any weapon that has the Two-handed special rule.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Aether-Shock Maul" typeId="1a1a-e592-2849-a5c0" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="ed07-dc69-062b-1aff">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="95ba-cda7-b831-6066">-</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="24d9-b8e1-a355-2458">+2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="f7a6-e0d8-7973-cd8d">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="2f86-c8b4-b3b4-3ff9">Melee, Deflagrate</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Twin-linked Storm Bolter" typeId="1a1a-e592-2849-a5c0" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="3db4-c0c5-2d5a-86c0">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="95ba-cda7-b831-6066">24</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="24d9-b8e1-a355-2458">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="f7a6-e0d8-7973-cd8d">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="2f86-c8b4-b3b4-3ff9">Assault 2, Twin-linked</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Rosarius" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="58a8-4d60-b4cc-1832">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with a Rosarius gains a 4+ Invulnerable Save. Invulnerable Saves granted by a Rosarius do not stack
with other Invulnerable Saves. If a model equipped with a Rosarius also has the Shield of Faith (X) special rule, the Rosarius instead changes the value in brackets of that special rule to 4+ (this is already included in the profile of models who have a Rosarius in their base wargear).</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Legatine" typeId="4bb2-cb95-e6c8-5a21" typeName="Unit" hidden="false" id="0597-c86e-c902-1704">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="ddd7-6f5c-a939-b69e">Infantry (Line)</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Move" typeId="893e-2d76-8f04-44e5">6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="WS" typeId="cc42-7ed5-7092-5c84">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="74ae-c840-0036-d244">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="e478-41d4-a092-48a8">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="T" typeId="c32b-5fdd-3fbe-9b1f">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="W" typeId="57ee-1126-32a9-5672">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="62d3-22d7-2d49-52dc">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="f111-2ce5-dd12-d6b0">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="e8a6-1da9-d384-8727">8</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Save" typeId="e593-6b3c-f169-04f0">3+</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Chirurgeon’s Tools" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="af49-ff67-6994-5def">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">All models with the Infantry unit Type in a unit that includes at least one model with Chirurgeon’s Tools gains the Feel No Pain (5+) special rule. Units that include more than one Chirurgeon’s Tools do not stack the Feel No Pain (X) special rule and gain no additional benefit. Models with the Artillery Sub-type are not affected by this special rule and do not gain
the Feel No Pain (X) special rule.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Sarissa" typeId="1a1a-e592-2849-a5c0" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="f8ca-a2c1-ea9a-8c61">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="95ba-cda7-b831-6066">-</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="24d9-b8e1-a355-2458">+1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="f7a6-e0d8-7973-cd8d">-</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="2f86-c8b4-b3b4-3ff9">Melee, Two-Handed</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Celestian" typeId="4bb2-cb95-e6c8-5a21" typeName="Unit" hidden="false" id="443e-06f6-e70a-d857">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="ddd7-6f5c-a939-b69e">Infantry (Line)</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Move" typeId="893e-2d76-8f04-44e5">6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="WS" typeId="cc42-7ed5-7092-5c84">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="74ae-c840-0036-d244">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="e478-41d4-a092-48a8">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="T" typeId="c32b-5fdd-3fbe-9b1f">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="W" typeId="57ee-1126-32a9-5672">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="62d3-22d7-2d49-52dc">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="f111-2ce5-dd12-d6b0">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="e8a6-1da9-d384-8727">8</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Save" typeId="e593-6b3c-f169-04f0">3+</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Neural Whip" typeId="1a1a-e592-2849-a5c0" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="233f-42e2-ee20-aa09">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="95ba-cda7-b831-6066">-</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="24d9-b8e1-a355-2458">+2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="f7a6-e0d8-7973-cd8d">-</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="2f86-c8b4-b3b4-3ff9">Melee, Deflagrate, Ritual Pair, Specialist Weapon</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Seraph" typeId="4bb2-cb95-e6c8-5a21" typeName="Unit" hidden="false" id="4dfd-15ec-9e95-9a2c">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="ddd7-6f5c-a939-b69e">Infantry</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Move" typeId="893e-2d76-8f04-44e5">6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="WS" typeId="cc42-7ed5-7092-5c84">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="74ae-c840-0036-d244">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="e478-41d4-a092-48a8">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="T" typeId="c32b-5fdd-3fbe-9b1f">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="W" typeId="57ee-1126-32a9-5672">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="62d3-22d7-2d49-52dc">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="f111-2ce5-dd12-d6b0">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="e8a6-1da9-d384-8727">7</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Save" typeId="e593-6b3c-f169-04f0">3+</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
  </sharedProfiles>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Attachment" id="91d2-0fc7-9dab-b23b" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="81">
      <description>A weapon with this special rule cannot be taken by a model on its own, and is always marked as “in-built” with another weapon on that model’s profile.
If a weapon with this special rule is in-built on a ranged weapon, then the model can always shoot with the exterminator in addition to that other weapon when it makes a Shooting Attack with that weapon without needing the Firing Protocols (X) special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Faithful Masses" id="3ed6-967d-7609-6f7b" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="82">
      <description>When a unit that is composed entirely of models with this special rule is selected as a Troops choice, then up to three such units may be selected to fill that Troops choice slot instead of only one (even if they have a different entry in the army list).
All units selected in this manner count as part of the same Troops choice for the purposes of Army Selection and Deployment only, when deployed onto the battlefield or into Reserves they are counted as a single unit and all units selected as part of the same Troops choice must be deployed at the same time (but are not required to deploy in proximity with each other) – and if placed into Reserves then all units in that choice must be placed into Reserves. Likewise, when making Reserves rolls one roll is made for all units selected as part of the same choice. 
Once deployed onto the battlefield, all units selected in this manner are treated as separate and distinct units or choices for any Primary or Secondary Objectives or other special rules and operate as separate units in all ways.
When assigning additional models to units (such as using the Monastic Envoys special rule), each unit selected using the Faithful Masses special rule is considered separate and may have models assigned to it as per the normal rules as the controlling player chooses.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="[Sororitas] Convent" id="1012-46a2-9038-fda4" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="81">
      <description>A [Sororitas] Convent is selected as any other unit, using up a single Force Organisation slot and bought in the same manner. However, before the first turn begins and any models are deployed to the battlefield, all models in a [Sororitas] Convent must be assigned to another unit from the same Detachment of the army they were selected as part of. Sisters [Sororitas] may only be assigned to units with the Infantry Unit Type and the Acts of Faith special rule, and may not join units that have the Mechanised or Monstrous sub-type. No Sister [Sororitas] may be assigned to any unit that includes one or more models with the Independent Character special rule or Unique Sub-type (but such models may join a unit that includes a Sister [Sororitas] as normal during either deployment or any following turn). No more than one Sister [Sororitas] may be assigned to any given unit.
Once assigned to a unit, the Sister [Sororitas] is considered part of that unit and may not leave it under any circumstances – if that unit is removed as a casualty then the Sister [Sororitas]is removed as well. In battles using Victory points, no Victory points are ever scored for removing a Sister [Sororitas] as a casualty. When assigned to a unit, a Sister [Sororitas] gains all of the special rules (with the exception of those that specifically forbid it) and Unit Sub-types listed for the unit to which it is attached, but does not gain access to any additional Wargear options available to the unit to which it is assigned.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Civil Order" id="ae9a-9fe4-4e98-ce69" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="81">
      <description>A unit with this special rule does not take up a Force Organisation slot as part of an Adepta Sororitas detachment, but may never be a Compulsory unit.
If your army includes at least one Adepta Sororitas detachment, then units with this special rule may be taken as non-compulsory Elite choices as part of any Imperialis Militia or Cult Imperialis detachments in your army. Models in units that are taken in this way lose the Acts of Faith special rule, and can be assigned to units without the Acts of Faith special rule, though all other rules and restrictions still apply.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dodge" id="2ce6-48cd-7f65-5fc2" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="81">
      <description>A model with this special rule has an invulnerable save equal to the value of X against melee attacks as well as against any shooting attacks made as part of a Reaction.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Litanies of the Faith (X)" id="0464-920f-5fa4-5d98" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="83">
      <description>A model with this special rule and the War Hymns (X) special rule selects a number of War Hymns equal to the X value of this special rule, rather than just one, and may recite a number of War Hymns each turn up to that same number, rather than just one.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Miraculous Intervention" id="a312-bfa8-7613-d89f" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="83">
      <description>The first time in each battle that a model with this special rule is reduced to 0 Wounds, it is not destroyed. Instead, place the model in reserves (it may not join a unit while in reserves) and it regains D3 Wounds.
At the start of the controlling player’s next turn, pick a point any where on the battlefield that is more than 9” from any enemy model and more than 1” from any table edge or Impassable Terrain, then the model takes a Leadership test.
If the test is failed then the chosen point is scattered as per the normal rules for Scatter. If it scatters onto Impassable Terrain, within 3” of an enemy model, or off of the edge of the battlefield, then your opponent can move the point any where on the battlefield that is more than 9” from any enemy model or Impassable Terrain. If the Check is passed then the point does not scatter.
Once the final location of the chosen point is determined, the model arrives from reserves. It is placed with its base centered on the chosen point, or as close as possible if impossible.
Once the model is placed on the battlefield, each enemy unit within 12” must take an immediate Pinning check. Any enemy unit that is not Pinned may then make the Interceptor Advanced Reaction targeting the model, as normal. The model may then act normally for the rest of the turn, including moving, shooting, and charging as normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Martyrdom" id="465a-170a-2ccb-3e0f" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="83">
      <description>If a model with this special rule is destroyed, friendly models with the Ministorum faction automatically pass any Morale and Pinning tests (but not any other kind of Leadership tests) they have to take, until the end of the current Phase</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mistress of Faith" id="725e-c092-4166-bfb0" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="83">
      <description>An army may only include a maximum of one model with this special rule per 1,000 points. This counts across all Detachments of an army. In addition, a model with this special rule may select a unit with the Sororitas Retinue special rule as part of the same Force Organization Slot.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Monastic Envoys" id="3ee6-a513-37e1-5ecd" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="83">
      <description>A Preacher Chorus is selected as any other unit, using up a single Force Organisation slot and bought in the same manner. However, before the first turn begins and any models are deployed to the battlefield, all models in a Preacher Chorus must be assigned to another unit from the same Detachment of the army they were selected as part of. Ministorum Preachers may only be assigned to units with the Infantry Unit Type, and may not join units that have the Mechanised or Monstrous sub-type. No Ministorum Preacher may be assigned to any unit that includes one or more models with the Independent Character special rule or Unique Sub-type (but such models may join a unit that includes a Ministorum Preacher as normal during either deployment or any following turn). No more than one Ministorum Preacher may be assigned to any given unit.
Once assigned to a unit, the Ministorum Preacher is considered part of that unit and may not leave it under any circumstances – if that unit is removed as a casualty then the Ministorum Preacher is removed as well. In battles using Victory points, no Victory points 
are ever scored for removing a Ministorum Preacher as a casualty. When assigned to a unit, a Ministorum Preacher gains all of the special rules (with the exception of those that specifically forbid it) and Unit Sub-types listed for the unit to which it is attached, but does not gain access to any additional Wargear options available to the unit to which it is assigned.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Pride of Place" id="feac-fee9-5b3e-ce2c" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="83">
      <description>A model with this special rule may not embark upon any model with the Transport Unit Sub-type, regardless of its Unit Type or any special rules the model with the Transport Sub-type may have.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rain of Death" id="6e31-2bb9-6872-c0ec" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="84">
      <description>Any Hits inflicted upon models with an Armour Value by a weapon with this special rule are always resolved against the model’s Side Armour Value.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Retaliation" id="c4a5-6467-b9ac-1870" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="84">
      <description>Attacks may only be made using weapons with this special rule as part of a Reaction and automatically hit the target unit without needing to roll To Hit</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ritual Pair" id="af2e-4da7-512f-7e5e" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="84">
      <description>A model that is equipped with two Melee weapons that have this special rule, and chooses one to fight with in close combat, receives +2 attacks instead of the usual +1 for fighting with two Melee weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sanctic" id="0074-7212-ce2a-38ac" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="84">
      <description>A weapon with this special rule always wounds models with the Daemon unit Type on a 2+ and any Invulnerable Save made by models with the Daemon unit Type against any Wounds it inflicts must be re-rolled.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shield of Faith (X)" id="3ae9-6d01-38e0-6452" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="84">
      <description>A model with this special rule gains an Invulnerable Save equal to the value listed in brackets.
When rolling a Shield of Faith Invulnerable Save, improve that Invulnerable Save by 1 step (from 6+ to 5+ for instance) if the wound being saved against was inflicted by any of the following:
• a Psychic Power;
• a model with the Daemon unit Type;
• a model with the Psyker or Corrupted unit Sub-type.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sudden Strike (X)" id="4262-5c8a-59e5-504e" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="84">
      <description>In a turn in which a model with this special rule Charges into combat, it adds a bonus to its Initiative Characteristic until the end of the Assault phase. The bonus added to the model’s Initiative is equal to the value in brackets after the special rule; for example, a model with Sudden Strike (2) adds a bonus of +2 to its Initiative.
A model that has made a Disordered Charge that turn receives no benefit from Sudden Strike (X).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sororitas Retinue" id="7afc-22db-ec44-a3c7" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="84">
      <description>A unit with this special rule may only be selected as part of a Detachment that includes at least one model with the Mistress of Faith special rule. A unit selected in this manner is considered a ‘Retinue Squad’ and the model with the Mistress of Faith special rule is referred to as the Retinue Squad’s Leader for the purposes of this special rule (if the Detachment includes more than one model with the Mistress of Faith special rule then the controlling player selects one as the unit’s Leader). The Retinue Squad does not use up a Force Organisation slot and is considered part of the same unit as the model selected as its Leader. The Retinue Squad must be deployed with the model selected as its Leader deployed as part of the unit and the Leader may not voluntarily leave the Retinue Squad during play. A unit that includes any models with this special rule may not be selected as part of an army without a Leader.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Supreme Leader" id="9ef6-24ec-7ffa-cec2" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="84">
      <description>A Detachment can only include one model with this special rule, which must be your Warlord if it is taken as part of a Primary Detachment.
In addition, if all models in the unit this model joins also have the Zealot special rule, then that unit gains the Fearless and Hatred (everything) special rules, even if the unit includes less than half of the models it started the battle with.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Passion" id="dbca-e840-7938-b69f" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="84">
      <description>A model with this special rule, and all models in its unit, gain the Hatred (everything) and Stubborn special rules.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Transport Bay" id="2257-ab16-1223-9759" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="84">
      <description>A model with this special rule may carry models of the Dreadnought and Automata Unit Types, as well as models with the Cavalry Unit Type but not the Antigrav Sub-type. Each Dreadnought model uses 10 points of Transport Capacity, while each Automata and Cavalry model uses up a number of Transport Capacity points equal to twice its starting Wounds Characteristic.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Voice of the Emperor" id="3328-c7bc-e662-cf45" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="85">
      <description>Whilst a model with this special rule is on the battlefield, the controlling player may attempt an additional Act of Faith in each of their turns.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Wrathful Blows (X)" id="c9e1-c5f4-444a-51eb" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="85">
      <description>A model making Attacks with a weapon with this special rule makes an amount of Attacks equal to the number shown in brackets, regardless of their Attacks Characteristic and any bonuses gained for Charging.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Zealot" id="07c6-e5d0-b8db-da29" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="85">
      <description>All models in a unit that includes only models with this special rule gains the Fearless and Hatred (everything) special rules so long as the unit includes at least half the models it started the battle with (not including any models that have joined the unit during play).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Acts of Faith" id="e07d-af0c-7db9-7cb3" hidden="false" publicationId="d640-eeef-2bd8-23c7" page="79">
      <description>A unit entirely comprised of models with the Act of Faith special rule may be selected to perform an Act of Faith during the controlling player’s turn, which grant specific benefits to the unit.
Unless otherwise specified, a player may only attempt one Act of Faith during each of their turn, regardless of wether or not it is succesful. This may be increased by special rules or effects in the same way as Reactions; however, a player may never attempt more than three Acts of Faith during each of their turns. Each unit may attempt no more than one Act of Faith during each turn; once a unit has attempted an Act of Faith, wether succesful or not, it cannot attempt to make any more Acts of Faith during that turn.
An Act of Faith is declared when a unit is selected for a specific action. Each Act of Faith indicates at the start of which action it may be performed, and under which condition. Unless otherwise specified, the effects of the Act of Faith last until the end of the phase in which it is performed.
When you declare that a unit attempts an Act of Faith, the unit takes a Leadership test. However, special rules that allow a model to modify or automatically pass Leadership tests have no effect on attempting an Act of Faith, unless otherwise specified. If the test is failed, the Act of Faith is not performed and grants no benefits, and the unit receives D3 Wounds against which only Invulnerable Saves may be taken (no Damage Mitigation rolls may be made to negate these Wounds). These Wounds are allocated in the same manner as those received during a Shooting Attack. Then proceed with the unit’s action as normal.
If the test is succesful, the unit receives the benefits of the Act of Faith.


Act of Faith: Holy Fusillade
Attempt this Act of Faith when a unit is selected to make a Shooting Attack. If succesful, apply the following modifiers to the unit’s Weapons until the end of the Shooting Phase, depending on the weapon’s Type:
• Bolt and/or Auto weapons: add 1 to the number of shots fired when making a Shooting Attack.
• Flame weapons: add 1 to the weapon’s Strength when making a Shooting Attack.
• Melta weapons: add 6” to the weapon’s Maximum Range when making a Shooting Attack.
If the unit makes shooting attacks with all three categories (Bolt and/or Auto weapons, Flame weapons, and Melta weapons) as part of that Shooting Attack, then those weapons additionally gain the Shred special rule until the end of the Shooting Phase.


Act of Faith: Light of the Emperor
Attempt this Act of Faith when a unit is selected to make a Shooting Attack. If succesful, the unit is no longer Pinned (if it was Pinned), and may immediately make an out-of-sequence Move of up to the highest Initiative value in the unit before it makes its Shooting Attack. Until the end of the Shooting Phase, all models in that unit gain the Relentless and Preferred Enemy (Everything) special rules.


Act of Faith: Hand of the Emperor
Attempt this Act of Faith when a unit is selected to make a Charge move. If succesful, enemy units may not declare Reactions against that charge, add +2 to the roll when determining Charge Distance, and all models in the unit gain the Furious Charge (1) special rule until the end of the Assault Phase. 


Act of Faith: Spirit of the Martyr
Attempt this Act of Faith when choosing a combat in which the unit is engaged. If succesful, all models in that unit gain +1 Attack and the Feel No Pain (3+) special rule until the end of the Assault Phase.


Act of Faith: Endless Crusade
Attempt this Act of Faith when the unit performs a Sweeping Advance. If succesful, the Falling Back unit is automatically caught by the Sweeping Advance and destroyed, without having to roll off with your opponent. When the unit Consolidates this turn, it may move up to a number of inches equal to its Movement characteristic plus its Initiative characteristic, instead of just its Initiative characteristic. 


Act of Faith: Divine Guidance
Attempt this Act of Faith when a friendly unit attempts to Regroup, before rolling to Regroup. If succesful, the unit automatically stops falling back and may act normally during the rest of the turn, including Moving, Running, and making Charge moves. It may shoot normally, but always count as having moved during that turn when making Shooting attacks. If failed, do not test to Regroup and the unit automatically continues Falling Back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Blessed Imagifier" id="4a71-d641-d5fe-f7fc" hidden="false">
      <description>All of the controlling player’s units with the Ministorum faction within 6” of a model with a Blessed Imagifier count their Leadership as being 10 when resolving Morale checks or Pinning checks, when reciting War Hymns, and when attempting Acts of Faith. In addition, all models in a unit that includes an Imagifier gain the Line Sub-type as long as they remain part of that unit – this benefit is lost immediately if the model with the Blessed Imagifier is removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Redemption in Death" id="cd96-5999-9ef5-b790" hidden="false">
      <description>If a model with this special rule that is engaged in close combat is reduced to 0 Wounds and destroyed, it is not removed from the battlefield if it has not yet made its Attacks in that phase. After the model has made all of its Attacks in that phase, or if the model is unable to make Attacks at the Initiative step in which it fights, remove it as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <catalogueLinks>
    <catalogueLink type="catalogue" name="New Catalogue (link)" id="56fe-6546-cd58-61e1" targetId="f84d-94cf-5ce6-b393"/>
  </catalogueLinks>
</catalogue>
